# .rag/.gitignore — commit the reproducible parts, ignore the rebuildable ones.
#
# Committed:  config.toml, .ragignore, requirements.txt, bootstrap.sh, mcp.json,
#             docs/, toolkit/, notebooks/, VERSION
#             so another machine can rebuild the same index.
# Ignored:    everything below — it is derived data, often gigabytes, and it is
#             machine-specific (model caches, absolute paths inside the store).
#
# NO TRAILING SLASHES on the four store entries. When the project sits in a
# file-sync container these are SYMLINKS to a store outside it, and a
# trailing-slash pattern matches directories only — `db/` would not match the
# symlink `db`, and git would commit a link to an absolute path that exists on
# exactly one machine.
#
# The same split applies twice over: whatever this file ignores must also stay
# out of the sync container. See references/cloud-synced-corpora.md.

.venv
cache
db
state

# ...and as real directories, for a workspace that was never relocated.
.venv/
cache/
db/
state/

__pycache__/
*.pyc
notebooks/.ipynb_checkpoints/
*.log
.DS_Store
